> ...it is not a good idea to quaff or read as-discovered unknown potions
> or scrolls.

Actually, I deliberately do that as fast as possible, when I'm as low
level as possible. Leads you to discover a lot of stuff, and at the
lower levels, you're less likely to be peeved that you died. And you're
less likely to run into anything immediately deadly. If I ran into
and unidentified object in the lower levels (when I was relatively high
level), of course, I'd be wary. But unidentified objects are generally
few and far between by that time.
